# A territory whose biome is ice.
#
# **`spec/planet.md`: *Each territory has a biome*, and *a biome earns its place by being shown
# rather than by being obeyed.*** So the whole of what there is to assert is that this is a world
# the engine accepts - `terrain` joins a territory to a biome and nothing obeys it.
#
# **No command, because zero is a cardinality.** Sean, 2026-10-02: *we support many commands, which
# does not seem substantively different than also supporting zero commands.* **A rule firing here
# would assert that one rule of sixteen leaves a terrain alone**, which is almost no evidence that
# none of them does, and would need a place and a unit that have nothing to do with a biome.
#
# **What it holds is the vocabulary.** `spec/data/schema.4x` declares `{biome id:3 name:ice}` and
# `{reference id:78 column:158 to:biome}`, so `is:ice` is refused the moment that row is deleted -
# which is what the mutation sweep found nothing doing: all six biomes with nothing referring to any
# of them, `C-218`. **One test per biome, because the vocabulary is six facts.**

{test name:a-territory-whose-biome-is-ice}

{given}
{territory id:1 name:territory-1}
{terrain of:territory-1 is:ice}

{then}
{territory id:1 name:territory-1}
{terrain of:territory-1 is:ice}
